.TH PRODIGY-PASSWORD-LCD-60S 1 "2026-07-29" "GWAY local tools" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
prodigy-password-lcd-60s \- show the current AP password on the local LCD
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B prodigy-password-lcd-60s
.RI [ --dry-run ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reads
.I /home/arthe/ap-password.txt
and writes a local LCD event lockfile that displays the AP password for
60 seconds. The command is intended for RFID mode bindings on gway-001.
.PP
The command does not print the password to standard output. It reports only the
SSID, LCD event id, display duration, and password length.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --dry-run
Validate inputs and report metadata without writing the LCD lockfile.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PRODIGY_PASSWORD_FILE
Override the password file path. Defaults to
.IR /home/arthe/ap-password.txt .
.TP
.B PRODIGY_PASSWORD_LCD_SECONDS
Override the display duration. Defaults to 60.
.TP
.B PRODIGY_PASSWORD_LCD_EVENT_ID
Override the LCD event id. Defaults to 12.
.TP
.B RFID_MODE_LCD_LOCK_DIR
LCD lockfile directory supplied by rfid-mode-runner.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rfid-arm-next-script (1),
.BR rfid-mode-runner (1),
.BR prodigy-ap-password (1)
